// The bass walks down the G major scale, G F# E D C B A, one note per bar, under G, G/F#, Em, D,
// C, C/B and Am. Pick the bass note on beat 1, then strum the top three strings D, D U, D U.
// G/F#: index on string 6 fret 2, its tip muting string 5. C/B: ring finger from fret 3 to fret 2.
\title "Slash chords: the bass walks down from G"
\tempo 80
\track ("Guitar" "Gtr.") { instrument acousticguitarsteel }
\staff { tabs }
\ts (4 4)
